WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.999
A hiring application needs proof of training, not your entire certificate. Facet keeps digital

00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:09.998
documents private and lets you approve exactly which signed facts an application can see.

00:00:10.548 --> 00:00:16.562
The wallet identifies the holder through a signed NEAR login. This capture uses an injected test

00:00:16.562 --> 00:00:21.449
wallet with a real signature and live holder binding. Manual wallet compatibility remains

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:21.825
unverified.

00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:28.225
I upload fictional training notes. The original is encrypted in my local vault. My password stays on

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:32.354
this device, and an encrypted backup preserves my documents and holder identity.

00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:39.274
A document NFT registers a salted fingerprint on NEAR. This self-recorded upload remains unverified.

00:00:39.274 --> 00:00:44.278
Registration alone does not authenticate a document or confer legal ownership.

00:00:44.828 --> 00:00:51.427
The demo academy now signs a training credential. Its claims carry a real BBS signature and a

00:00:51.427 --> 00:00:54.921
holder-bound NEAR record. The academy and qualification are fictional.

00:00:55.471 --> 00:01:00.641
The application requests course and completion. Before approving, I see those exact fields. Name,

00:01:00.641 --> 00:01:06.550
score, date and student reference stay hidden. The request also binds its purpose and a single-use

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:06.919
nonce.

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:13.285
I approve and export a selective proof. A separate browser imports it without my vault or original

00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:16.707
document. The exported package excludes the hidden name and score.

00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:22.438
Verification succeeds. The application sees Data Privacy Foundations and Completed, alongside

00:01:22.438 --> 00:01:28.560
required public credential bindings. A real testnet transaction records the verification receipt and

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.444
consumes the request nonce.

00:01:30.994 --> 00:01:36.705
NEAR anchors issuer keys, expiry, revocation and nonce use. Signature and disclosure checks run

00:01:36.705 --> 00:01:42.008
outside the contract. This gives applications a shared source of current credential status.

00:01:42.558 --> 00:01:48.830
I prepare a fresh unused proof, then revoke the credential on NEAR. That proof is now rejected

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.151
because of revocation. Revocation cannot erase facts already shared.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:57.438
For agents, this permission preview selects only course and completion. The planned delivery

00:01:57.438 --> 00:02:02.539
contains an approved presentation, keeping the original document and holder key private. This screen

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.360
does not create a grant.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:10.511
The preview limits access to ten minutes and two executions. NEAR enforces signed permissions,

00:02:10.511 --> 00:02:16.111
usage, expiry and revocation. An agent can consume an existing capability without receiving the

00:02:16.111 --> 00:02:16.911
vault password.

00:02:17.461 --> 00:02:23.883
An optional OutLayer TEE copy stores the approved document, credential and holder key in sealed

00:02:23.883 --> 00:02:29.021
storage. NEAR authorizes private execution and wallet recovery. Plaintext documents are excluded

00:02:29.021 --> 00:02:30.733
from public chain records.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:37.216
Separate live tests passed TEE storage, agent delivery and recovery. The complete private browser

00:02:37.216 --> 00:02:42.301
workflow remains incomplete because some callbacks expire before settlement. This walkthrough shows

00:02:42.301 --> 00:02:45.691
agent previews, not a completed private agent run.

00:02:46.241 --> 00:02:51.423
The published contract and worker fingerprints make the integration inspectable. The TEE delivers

00:02:51.423 --> 00:02:57.005
browser-prepared proofs, and the demo agent uses deterministic checks. Try Facet and review the

00:02:57.005 --> 00:02:58.600
public code and evidence.
